  "content": {
    "id": "p33-q2-node",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Let $y=(f(x))^2$. This is usually differentiated using the chain rule. Would splitting it as $y=f(x)\\times f(x)$ then using the product rule give the same result?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Yes. Both methods give $y'=2f(x)f'(x)$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y'&=f'(x)f(x)+f(x)f'(x)\\\\y'&=2f(x)f'(x).\\end{align*}$$\nThe chain rule gives the same result.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 28
  },
